# 9. EKS Networking

EKS uses AWS VPC networking.

Components:

```text
VPC

|

Subnets

|

Security Groups

|

Elastic Network Interfaces

|

Pods
```

---

# 10. EKS Recommended VPC Design

Production architecture:

```text
                 Internet

                    |

              Load Balancer

                    |

        -------------------------

        Public Subnets


        -------------------------

        Private Subnets


        EC2 Worker Nodes

        Pods
```

---

# 11. Availability Zones

Production clusters should use multiple AZs.

Example:

```text
VPC

|

├── AZ-A

│    └── Worker Nodes

│

├── AZ-B

│    └── Worker Nodes

│

└── AZ-C

     └── Worker Nodes
```

Benefits:

* Fault tolerance
* High availability

---

# 12. Amazon VPC CNI

EKS uses the AWS VPC CNI plugin.

It allows Pods to receive VPC IP addresses.

Example:

```text
Worker Node

10.0.1.10


Pod

10.0.1.20


Pod

10.0.1.30
```

Pods communicate using AWS networking.

---

# 13. Security Groups in EKS

Security Groups control network access.

Example:

Worker node security group:

Allow:

```text
HTTPS

443

From Load Balancer
```

Allow:

```text
Kubernetes API

443

From Admin Network
```

