# 14. IAM Integration with EKS

EKS uses AWS IAM for authentication.

Flow:

```text
User

↓

IAM Authentication

↓

Kubernetes RBAC

↓

Permission Granted
```

---

# 15. IAM Roles for Service Accounts (IRSA)

IRSA allows Kubernetes Pods to use AWS permissions securely.

Without IRSA:

```text
Application

↓

AWS Access Keys

↓

S3
```

Problem:

Credentials stored inside application.

---

With IRSA:

```text
Pod

↓

Service Account

↓

IAM Role

↓

AWS Service
```

Example:

A Pod needs S3 access:

```text
Application Pod

↓

IAM Role

↓

Amazon S3
```

